WEBVTT

1
00:00:04.400 --> 00:00:08.208
Some materials come from nature.
Others are made by people.

2
00:00:08.428 --> 00:00:12.375
You will test materials, and
find out why each one is chosen.

3
00:00:12.875 --> 00:00:16.962
Wood comes from trees. It
grows, so it is natural.

4
00:00:17.182 --> 00:00:22.012
Wool comes from sheep. It grows, and
is cut off and spun. It is natural.

5
00:00:22.232 --> 00:00:25.947
Stone is dug out of the
ground. It is natural too.

6
00:00:26.167 --> 00:00:31.043
A natural material grows, or it
is dug up. People do not make it.

7
00:00:31.543 --> 00:00:36.512
Plastic, glass, brick and paper
are made by people, in factories.

8
00:00:36.732 --> 00:00:41.516
Glass is made by melting sand,
very hot. The sand becomes glass.

9
00:00:41.736 --> 00:00:45.404
Paper is made in a factory,
by mashing wood into pulp.

10
00:00:45.624 --> 00:00:49.943
These are manufactured: made by
people, usually in a factory.

11
00:00:50.163 --> 00:00:54.947
To sort a material, ask one question:
could you find it in nature?

12
00:00:55.447 --> 00:00:59.719
A property is what a material is
like. You can test for each one.

13
00:00:59.939 --> 00:01:06.441
Test the glass. Press it: it
is hard. Bend it: it is stiff.

14
00:01:06.661 --> 00:01:12.094
Hold it to the light: it is see-through.
Pour water on it: waterproof.

15
00:01:12.314 --> 00:01:16.680
Glass is hard, stiff, see-through
and waterproof, all at once.

16
00:01:16.900 --> 00:01:21.869
Now test wool. It is soft, and it
bends easily. Different answers!

17
00:01:22.089 --> 00:01:25.990
Each test finds one property.
A material has several.

18
00:01:26.490 --> 00:01:29.090
Drip water on glass,
and the water runs off.

19
00:01:29.310 --> 00:01:32.375
Drip water on wool,
and the water soaks in.

20
00:01:32.595 --> 00:01:35.939
Glass is waterproof: water
does not go through it.

21
00:01:36.159 --> 00:01:38.899
Wool is absorbent: it soaks water up.

22
00:01:39.119 --> 00:01:43.902
You will record each result in
a table. Glass: yes. Wool: no.

23
00:01:44.122 --> 00:01:47.698
Fill in a row for every material.
Then you can compare them.

24
00:01:48.198 --> 00:01:51.913
People choose a material for a
job because of its properties.

25
00:01:52.133 --> 00:01:56.220
A kettle is metal, because metal
does not melt when it gets hot.

26
00:01:56.440 --> 00:02:01.223
Its handle is plastic. Plastic does
not carry the heat to your hand.

27
00:02:01.443 --> 00:02:05.809
A tyre is rubber. Rubber grips
the road and bends over bumps.

28
00:02:06.029 --> 00:02:10.765
Every material is chosen for its
properties. Science explains why.

29
00:02:11.265 --> 00:02:17.024
Natural materials grow, or are dug
up. People make the manufactured ones.

30
00:02:17.244 --> 00:02:21.795
A property is what a material is
like. Each test finds one of them.

31
00:02:22.015 --> 00:02:27.495
Glass is waterproof. Wool is
absorbent. You record both in a table.

32
00:02:27.715 --> 00:02:32.777
Every material is chosen for its
properties. Now go on a hunt of your own!
